    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d705">

                <pb facs="0816" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.67/12–948: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-09">December 9,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received December 29—12:46 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–1230. Re Embtel 2751, November 27. Subject Dairen couriers having arisen during
                    general talk today, Embassy’s Counselor<anchor n="32" xml:id="d705-f1"/>
                    informed Chief American Section Ministry of Foreign Affairs that while we regard
                    despatch couriers via Vladivostok as less satisfactory to both Governments than
                    use of unarmed naval vessels, we are prepared to continue former method, but
                    would expect Soviet authorities, especially at Vladivostok, to facilitate travel
                    our couriers. Ministry official promised to take measures to this effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d705-f1" n="32" xml:id="d705-f1-content">
